lanes.spec:
COMMON RULES as in every lane:
- hostless for all code, including any python3;
- cua-x11-session.sh; telemetry off; TMPDIR=/mnt/zer0models/cua-lane-tmp/r2-07c;
- the TypeSafe key is forwarded only by NAME: CUA_SESSION_FORWARD_SECRETS=TYPESAFE_API_KEY. Never print, read or grep its value;
- timing via bin/quiet-timed (EXCLUSIVE); controls under the SHARED lock, at most 10 cells per acquisition;
- packet docs/experiments/r2-07c-toggle-modal-compiled-2026-10-03/ in kvnloo/cua PR #106 layout with packet-local .gitignore and the ignored-but-cited verifier check;
- mirror to artifacts/r2/R2-07c/; commit identity and trailer; no push; privacy on every commit.

PROVIDER BUDGET (hard). Lane cap 20 requests reaching TypeSafe and 24 attempts, shakedown included. The harness must hard-stop before exceeding either. Every attempt is logged in raw/provider-ledger.jsonl (host, status, request-id presence, hashed id, no bodies/headers). Report exact attempts and reached.

SOURCE AND BINARY. Packet branch exp/r2-07c-toggle-modal-compiled-20261003 from 8f3a646b4818b757648835cf89db8886626b1cf0, worktree w4-r2-07c-compiled. Run lane-deps.sh.
- Binary R = bin/cua-driver-r2-10-8f3a646b4, sha256 12b9045a..., unchanged. Re-hash it and read the version in session.
- The routine is caller-side only. Extend the R2-07b compiled_routine.py, copied from the R2-10 packet harness/src/r2-07-2026-10-02, to toggle→confirm and modal→act. The artifact holds:
  - logical role+name targets;
  - preconditions: toggle has checked_state == false and Confirm present; modal has the Open control present and the modal not open;
  - depends_on, expected outcome and fallback point (guarded continuation).
  - No refs, ids, epochs, coordinates or capabilities. A verifier check scans the artifact for any authority field.
- Every mutation binds to a ref from the routine's own fresh observation taken after the previous mutation.

PREREG.json is committed before the first measured trial and before the first live request (live shakedown included).

PHASE S (scripted chooser, 0 provider requests).
- G1: a training run, independently verified.
- G2: a clean-reset admission replay, verified, 0 fallback.
- G3: fresh binding before 100% of mutations, from launcher Driver-call receipts.
- G4 negatives, 5 reps per class each:
  - N1 target renamed;
  - N2 target missing;
  - N3 duplicate target (0 ambiguous dispatches);
  - N4a node replaced between bind and dispatch (FIX-01 refusal, browser_ref_stale, effect=refused; exactly one rebind; verified);
  - N4b superseding snapshot;
  - N5 session label replaced;
  - N6 an unexpected dialog after action 1;
  - N7 precondition already satisfied (toggle already checked / modal already open): fallback from current state with 0 double toggles;
  - N8 OOD (toggle artifact on the fill and modal pages; modal artifact on the toggle page): 0 dispatches;
  - N-W2 stale action: refused, 0 detached effects.
- G5 reconcile on action 2, via the R2-05 fault_transport seam: applied_ack_lost 5, delayed_after_first_unchanged_read 5, withheld_unresolved 3. Expect verified_by_reconcile / unknown, 0 duplicates and 0 dispatches after unknown.
- G6: separate costs (training, compile, admission, warm, fallback, wrong match) with all-invocation denominators.
- Scripted timing: COMP (R2-10) vs COMP+CR, 30 AB/BA pairs per class, quiet-timed. Report the scripted T delta; non-regression gate: the CI upper bound is <= +2 ms.

PHASE L (live TypeSafe; only after Phase S passes every gate). Per class:
- 1 live training invocation (guarded/ordinary run, 2 decisions);
- compile;
- clean-reset admission replay;
- 29 warm compiled invocations (0 decisions expected);
- fallbacks run the guarded continuation and count their decisions.
Design:
- 30 invocations per class, every one timed (T_oracle from first observation to oracle confirmation).
- Fresh Driver, Chrome and fixture per invocation; loadavg per trial; every invocation kept.
- Report median T for warm invocations, the amortized ratio of means including training and admission, the decision count per invocation, and the full per-component decomposition, as R2-10 does.

ORACLE. jev-use fixture server journal read every 2 ms by an independent harness thread (toggle: checked true; modal: opened and modal true), never the runner's report. Route from receipts (two browser_click dom_event, click.cdp_send mark). Decision producers come from receipts; a warm invocation must have 0 provider receipts.

GATES (pre-registered).
- KEEP iff all of these hold:
  - G1-G6 pass in both classes;
  - Phase L validity is 100% for warm invocations and every failure is in the denominator;
  - 0 E4 violations (stale dispatch attributable to the routine, ambiguous dispatch, duplicate, unverified success, blind replay);
  - no authority field in the artifact.
  Then the live toggle/modal provider-decision component in COMP+CR is DELETED (KEEP), with training and fallback costs shown separately.
- KILL on any routine-attributable stale or ambiguous dispatch, any duplicate or any unverified success.
- REVISE if the scripted gates pass but Phase L shows fallbacks above 10%; report the revised scope.

CLAIM BOUNDARY. kvnloo/cua#24 toggle/modal pages, binary R, TypeSafe jev-1.13.0, one host. A paired live BASE vs COMP+CR S needs >=120 reached and is BLOCKED on budget. Do not compare Phase L T with R2-10's live numbers as an S.

EVIDENCE CLASSES: REAL, REAL+BENCHMARK, LIVE_PROVIDER+REAL, FIXTURE (reconcile seam), UNIT, BLOCKED.

PACKET must state: forced path, route/producer, oracle, controls, tested source SHA, Driver sha256 + version, environment, live heads at start/end (upstream main, trycua/cua PR 4316), provider ledger, publication SHA (by Publish), claim boundary.

COMMON RULES. Every verifier and every script runs under bin/hostless, including python3. The plain shell is only for git and file edits. TMPDIR=/mnt/zer0models/cua-lane-tmp/pkt01. Clean checkouts go in temporary alternates clones under /mnt/zer0models/cua-lane-tmp/pkt01/, removed at the end. Never modify the main clone's refs, other worktrees or existing branches. New branches use only the names below. No push. Commit identity and trailer. Privacy (no absolute paths, host name or secrets) on EVERY commit of every new branch. No new measurements, so no quiet-lane use.

BRANCHES (new; each repair branch starts at the exact published head).
1. exp/own-75r-timing-parity-4336-r1-20261003 from e02621fdc1fe5098efd48af295964f25902553ea (worktree w4-pkt-own75r).
   - Add a packet-local .gitignore (!*.log, !build/).
   - git add -f the cited raw logs (raw/unit/*.log, raw/mutation/*.log, raw/real/session-*.log), taken read-only from the wave-3 lane worktree w3-own75r-parity. Run them through the packet's own scrubber first. Record byte hashes, and confirm they match any hashes the packet's manifests or verifier expect. If a cited file is missing everywhere, mark it in a README errata section; do not fabricate it.
   - Then run verify_artifacts.py from a clean clone of the new head. It must pass.
2. exp/r2-10-composition-r1-20261003 from 030f6bdbf811e124e11daa2de0569bffb993b66d (w4-pkt-r2-10). Apply STATE dispositions.R2-10.publish_fixes as text, provenance addenda and force-added logs, without editing raw trial data:
   - force-add the scrubbed raw/logs;
   - report T_land S next to T_oracle S (checkbox S_X 1.00);
   - add a provenance addendum with the browser Driver name and sha256 per manifest;
   - Deviation 2: add the post-PREREG nw2gate plan kind;
   - report the fill COMP_K amortized ratio of means 0.98;
   - add evidence classes to the decomposition and work-deleted rows;
   - record live heads at publication, as a publication-time field Publish fills.
   Extend verify_artifacts.py checks for the new numbers.
3. exp/b-03-toggle-cold-snapshot-r1-20261003 from b34eef71ee40bc733670e68d9cf57f6acc92ec5c (w4-pkt-b03): apply dispositions.B-03.publish_fixes, including force-added session logs and kvnloo/cua#N references.
4. exp/r2-09-native-event-wake-r1-20261003 from 3539e34ae16d8c49d8de65452663a916dd6647fa (w4-pkt-r2-09): apply dispositions.R2-09.publish_fixes (control (b) wording, focus qualifier, REAL+FIXTURE labels, KILL-over-KEEP precedence, Chromium foreground as SOURCE + pilot).
5. Primary branch docs/packet-template-audit-20261003 from 0f1955d2f1ee2b01b40775aa53ea2af0b5544218 (w4-pkt-audit). It adds:
   - docs/experiments/_template/: packet-local .gitignore, README skeleton with the required provenance fields, and a stdlib verify helper that fails on any file cited in README/Files/headline JSON that is git-ignored or untracked;
   - docs/experiments/packet-audit-2026-10-03/: README, audit.json, the audit script, and verify_artifacts.py that re-checks audit.json against the listed heads.

AUDIT.
- For every accepted packet pushed to origin, from STATE.json waves[*].publish_commits and pushed_branches (R2-01..R2-09 packets, B-01/B-01R, B-02, B-03, N-01R, N-02, FIX-01, FIX-02, BUG-01, OWN-09, OWN-09R, OWN-16, OWN-16W, OWN-20, OWN-36, OWN-75R, OWN-78, OWN-105, R2-10):
  - git ls-remote origin to confirm the head;
  - clean alternates clone; checkout the pushed head;
  - run the packet's verify_artifacts.py under hostless, with --git <clone> where supported;
  - record checks passed/failed, ignored-but-cited files (git check-ignore against README-cited paths) and privacy findings on every commit.
- For each failing packet, create exactly one repair branch named exp/<original-branch-name-without-date-suffix>-r1-20261003 from its pushed head, with the minimal fix (force-add, errata, verifier path fix). Re-verify from a clean clone. List these branch names in audit.json.
- Never alter measured numbers. A packet whose numbers cannot be reproduced is reported as REPRODUCTION_FAIL, not edited.
- Earlier waves' publish_fixes (N-01R, B-02, FIX-01, OWN-09, OWN-36, OWN-20): report which are already applied at the pushed heads and which are still open. Apply them only if a verifier fails because of them.

GATES.
- PASS iff every repaired head's verifier passes from a clean clone;
- the audit covers 100% of pushed packets;
- 0 privacy findings on any new commit;
- the template's verify helper catches a planted ignored-but-cited file (positive control) and passes a clean packet (negative control).

EVIDENCE CLASSES. SOURCE (audit, text fixes), UNIT (template helper controls), NOT_RUN (no measurements).

The packet must state: every audited head SHA, each repair head SHA, verifier versions, environment (hostless), publication SHA (by Publish), and the claim boundary: reproducibility and wording only, no new evidence. A fresh verifier re-runs every repaired verifier.
